SM-T715 tablet: the Mobile data tile back, through NetworkManager.

The modem runs on arm64 now (t715-modem: shannond serves ModemManager, so
NetworkManager sees it), so the tile is back in the catalogue and the default
layout (after Bluetooth, as on the 0.2.94 build), driven through
NetworkManager's gsm connection (t715-mobile) instead of the Pixel's
omamobile-sit: tile-state.sh probes nmcli, tile-action.sh brings the
connection up or down. The tile's signal bars (TilesModel.dataIcon) come from
tile-state.sh's data_signal and the technology from data_status, both read
from shannond's `shannonctl status` -- the same answers its ModemManager
facade gives; data=none without a gsm device or connection. Every nmcli probe
this patch adds runs with LC_ALL=C (the session is French, where nmcli says
"activé"; the hotspot probe upstream already had matches only the
connection's name, which nmcli does not localize). test/tile-scripts.sh and
test/tiles-model.js follow. Ported from
the armv7h series' 0004-tablet-modem (omamobile-shell 0.2.94). Against
omarchy-mobile 8991845 (omamobile-shell 0.2.147), after 0001-0009; 0.2.147's
data probe still reads omamobile-sit's state file plus its modem-refused
marker and modem switch (Pixel pieces), which this replaces.

